invariant: INV-26
file: quic_packet.c
catches: test/lint-quic-surface.sh
reason: quic_packet.c includes quic_aes_key.h, which gives it the body of
  aes_public_key and with it the ability to declare a key and write a
  traffic secret into a field of one. The compiler refuses that edit in
  every source that does not include the header, so the include is the
  one line that undoes INV-26's structural check. It compiles, so
  nothing else in the build objects; tools/quic-footprint.py's
  key_holders() is what reads the include list, and
  `make lint-quic-surface` is where it runs.

--- old
#include "quic_packet.h"
--- new
#include "quic_packet.h"
#include "quic_aes_key.h"
